---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = "/guides/pricing-models";
const title = "Shopify Email Pricing Models \u2014 Build a Comparable Quote";
const desc = "Compare email quotes using billable definitions, send projections, peak demand and full transition costs.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Is per-send pricing always cheaper?",
    "answer": "No. Compare the complete quote at the same workload and required features, including minimums, overages and peak months."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can engagement ratio predict the cheapest platform?",
    "answer": "It is one workload descriptor. It does not replace billable definitions, cadence, tier rules or feature requirements."
  },
  {
    "question": "What belongs in first-year cost?",
    "answer": "Recurring fees, modules, channels, implementation, migration, parallel operation and relevant exit charges. Label internal labor assumptions."
  },
  {
    "question": "Are the example amounts vendor prices?",
    "answer": "No. The two quotes and their crossover are hypothetical arithmetic examples only."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16">
    <a class="link" href="/guides">← All operator guides</a>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-6 max-w-5xl">{title}</h1>
    <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9">{desc}</p>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify ledger-card">
    <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black">Compare a defined workload</h2>
    <p>This guide is for the person approving a purchase or renewal. Obtain dated written quotes for the same workload rather than comparing advertised entry tiers. Record currency, taxes, billing period, contract length, renewal date, included features and quote expiry. This page supplies a costing method, not current vendor prices. Sequenzy belongs in the same quote worksheet as other candidates; no supplier is assumed cheapest.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify ledger-card">
    <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black">Separate the billable units</h2>
    <p>For each quote ask what counts as a billable contact, whether suppressed or inactive records count, how peaks are measured and when tiers reset. For sending, distinguish included messages, excess sends, transactional traffic and channel charges. For SMS obtain the applicable destination and message-segment rules instead of treating recipients as billable messages. Note minimum commitments and feature gates. Engagement ratios can describe the audience but cannot establish a universal pricing crossover.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify ledger-card">
    <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black">Build monthly workload rows</h2>
    <p>Use one row per planning month: start and end contacts, billable contacts under each quote, campaign recipients times campaign frequency, automation entrants times expected messages, transactional volume, channel usage and connected apps. Model baseline and peak months separately. Use actual logs where available and label unlaunched-flow estimates. Do not assume all eligible customers receive every flow step; purchases and exclusions can change volume. Reconcile the projected sends to an existing invoice before forecasting growth.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify ledger-card">
    <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black">Calculate full cost</h2>
    <p>For each month add the applicable platform tier, overages, channel fees, required modules and connected tools. Add onboarding, migration and implementation work separately so first-year cost is visible. Internal hours times a stated loaded hourly rate are a planning assumption, not free labor. Include parallel subscriptions and exit fees during transition. Avoid double counting a bundled module. Keep uncertain charges as ranges and request clarification before commitment.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify ledger-card">
    <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black">Hypothetical break-even example</h2>
    <p>These invented quotes illustrate arithmetic only; they are not prices for any named product. Assume Quote A costs $300 per month plus $0.002 per send, and Quote B costs $500 per month with all modeled sends included. Ignore taxes and other charges for this example. At 60,000 sends A is $420 and B is $500. At 140,000 sends A is $580 and B is $500. The simplified crossover is ($500 − $300) ÷ $0.002 = 100,000 sends. A real tier, cap or feature difference changes that equation.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify ledger-card">
    <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black">Test the commercial decision</h2>
    <p>Recompute costs when contacts grow but send frequency stays flat, when sends rise without new contacts, and when a peak campaign crosses a tier. Check whether annual commitment savings survive the peak month and whether unused allowance expires. Compare the cost of a required capability with the operating work needed without it. Keep any expected revenue benefit separate: a vendor-attributed order total is not evidence that a cheaper or richer plan caused incremental profit.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify ledger-card">
    <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black">Preserve records while changing billing exposure</h2>
    <p>Ask the vendor how suppression, archiving and deletion affect both invoices and operational records. Do not delete consent or suppression evidence merely to reach a lower tier. Confirm which exports remain available after cancellation and who will retain them under the store’s policy. If a lower tier removes workflow controls or data history, price that loss explicitly rather than treating the new invoice as like-for-like savings.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify ledger-card">
    <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black">Make renewal review actionable</h2>
    <p>Attach the quote, workload assumptions, invoice reconciliation and sensitivity results to the decision. Name an owner for each unresolved fee and record when notice is due. Re-model after material workload or contract changes, not only on an arbitrary calendar. The decision record should state the selected capability set, expected total cost, uncertainty range and the event that would trigger reconsideration. Use the migration guide to estimate transition work before calling a price delta a saving.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><p>Related: <a class="link" href="/guides/implementation-plan">Shopify Email Implementation Plan</a> · <a class="link" href="/guides/migration">Shopify Email Migration</a> · <a class="link" href="/guides/replenishment-tools">Shopify Replenishment Tools</a></p></section>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} />
</BaseLayout>
